WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.229 --> 00:00:04.910
Now that we have created our project

2
00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:08.429
and got the initial setup and imported our assets,

3
00:00:08.429 --> 00:00:10.269
we're gonna transition into talking

4
00:00:10.269 --> 00:00:13.750
about the landscape material creation.

5
00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:15.509
Now, before we get into this,

6
00:00:15.509 --> 00:00:18.309
each project's approach to creating a landscape

7
00:00:18.309 --> 00:00:20.109
is going to be different.

8
00:00:20.109 --> 00:00:23.670
You can use a different collection of methods,

9
00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:26.989
all dependent on the workflows for your project.

10
00:00:26.989 --> 00:00:28.910
Now, this particular example

11
00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:30.030
that we're gonna be going over today

12
00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.870
is gonna use this type of setup.

13
00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:33.630
We're gonna have a procedural layout

14
00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:35.789
based on the slope of the landscape

15
00:00:35.789 --> 00:00:38.030
that will expose different materials,

16
00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:42.090
that will expose different textures in our material

17
00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:45.030
in order to highlight where different surfaces are.

18
00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.929
We're going to also have textures

19
00:00:46.929 --> 00:00:49.270
that are for close-up detail

20
00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:52.170
and textures that are for far away detail

21
00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:55.140
to help reduce tiling artifacts.

22
00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.700
We're also gonna introduce hand painting,

23
00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:58.700
but we're gonna do it

24
00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.340
so that we can actually remove

25
00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.500
the procedurally placed grass

26
00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.859
so we have a little bit more control over where it is,

27
00:01:05.859 --> 00:01:08.180
but more importantly, where it is not.

28
00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:10.900
Finally, we're gonna add displacement to all of this

29
00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:15.019
to really help our landscape's surface stand out

30
00:01:15.019 --> 00:01:18.980
with Nanite and the new Nanite tessellation options.
